	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Measurement made using a temperature probe (e.g. thermistor) which is the
sum of the ambient air temperature plus the heat of friction caused by the high
speed air passing over the probe.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">TOTAL TEMPERATURE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx5"/>
