	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A small mass of air (whirlwind) that spins rapidly about an almost
vertical axis and forms a funnel cloud that contacts the ground; appears
as a pendant from a cumulonimbus cloud and is potentially the most
destructive of all weather systems.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
