	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">"Fluvial landforms" are features on the Earth's surface produced by the action, i.e. erosion and deposition, of a stream or river and include such landforms as bars, levees, braided and meandering channels, and alluvial fans.  "Fluvial processes" are those processes included in the action of running water in a stream or river</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
