	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">In radiation transfer, reflectance is the fraction of incoming radiation&#xD;
that is reflected from a medium. The sum of this, the transmittance, and&#xD;
the absorptance must equal unity.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">REFLECTANCE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx64"/>
</rdf:Description>

