	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-03-07 10:07:42.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Any radioactive form of a chemical element, having the same atomic weight as that element (i.e. same number of protons), but a different number of neutrons. Used in a variety of oceanic applications such as dating and
movement of water masses.); 
update Definition (Adapted from: Webster's College Dictionary. 1991. Random House.  ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Any radioactive form of a chemical element, having the same atomic weight as that element (i.e. same number of protons), but a different number of neutrons. Used in a variety of oceanic applications such as dating and
movement of water masses.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">RADIOISOTOPES</prefLabel>
