	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Radiocarbon refers to radioactive carbon especially carbon-14, but also
carbon-10 and carbon-12. Carbon-14 is a heavy radioactive isotope of Carbon
having a mass of 14 and a half-life of 5730 +/-40 years. Carbon-14 is useful in
dating organic materials during the last 50,000 years.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">RADIOCARBON</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx90"/>
</rdf:Description>

