<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d138302a-03b3-4cf7-95db-ac98f863c04f">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/959f1861-a776-41b1-ba6b-d23c71d4d1eb"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2016-04-04 09:04:46.0 [gee-cee] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (WETLANDS [d138302a-03b3-4cf7-95db-ac98f863c04f,85265] - SURFACE WATER FEATURES [959f1861-a776-41b1-ba6b-d23c71d4d1eb,158825]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2016-04-04 09:44:13.0 [gee-cee]  
update Definition (Wetlands is a term for a broad group of wet habitats. They are transitional lands between terrestrial and aquatic ecosystems where the lands may be permanently or intermittently water covered.); 
update Definition (National Research Council. 1992. Restoration of Aquatic Ecosystems. National Academy Press.  ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Wetlands is a term for a broad group of wet habitats. They are transitional lands between terrestrial and aquatic ecosystems where the lands may be permanently or intermittently water covered.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">WETLANDS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx94"/>
</rdf:Description>

