update Definition (Acid deposition is rain or snow that has a lower pH than precipitation from unpolluted skies. Acid deposition can also include dry forms of deposition such as nitrate and sulfate particles); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Acid deposition is rain or snow that has a lower pH than precipitation from unpolluted skies. Acid deposition can also include dry forms of deposition such as nitrate and sulfate particles</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
