	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Fossil fuel burning refers to the burning of any one of the organic fuels (coal, natural gas, oil, tar sands, and oil shale) derived from once living plants or animals.</definition>
