	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The alkalinity of seawater is the combined negative charges due to&#xD;
hydrogen carbonate and carbonate ions expressed in molal concentrations.&#xD;
Alkalinity is based on seawater being electrically neutral and is&#xD;
determined by titration (and therefore given the subscript t).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ALKALINITY</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx107"/>
</rdf:Description>

