</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2019-07-15 08:01:47.0 [mmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (Phenological Changes [cc5ab64b-11d0-4196-b7b3-f9c61e5e3ac6,368931] - BIOSPHERIC INDICATORS [76943142-e5a9-4ecf-b496-050dd3d97101,87035]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2019-07-15 08:03:50.0 [mmorahan] Rename Concept 
update PrefLabel (PHENOLOGICAL CHANGES); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Changes in the temporal pattern of seasonal life cycle events in plants
and animals, such as timing of blooming, hibernation, and migration.
Some phenological responses are triggered by mean temperature,
while others are more responsive to day length or weather. Changes in
phenology affect the growing season and, thus, ecosystem functioning
and productivity.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PHENOLOGICAL CHANGES</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx110"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/c6f81edb-b683-4356-93e6-5852766a5ee8"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/f73cf4ee-2ae0-47b0-a294-5f8a8f694215"/>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PHENOLOGICAL SHIFTS</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

