add broader relation (ANIMAL PHENOLOGICAL CHANGES [f73cf4ee-2ae0-47b0-a294-5f8a8f694215,368935] - PHENOLOGICAL CHANGES [cc5ab64b-11d0-4196-b7b3-f9c61e5e3ac6,368931]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Changes in the timing of periodic biological phenomena in animals,
such as hibernation, reproduction, and migration, that are correlated
with climatic conditions.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ANIMAL PHENOLOGICAL CHANGES</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx817"/>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ANIMAL PHENOLOGICAL SHIFTS</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx110">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<text xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" xml:lang="en">Adapted from the USGCRP Glossary (https://www.globalchange.gov/climate-change/glossary) and the European Environment Agency Phenology of plant and animal species (https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/indicators/plant-phenology-2) indicator</text>
</rdf:Description>

