	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">RESTORATION: The processes by which an area is treated in  an attempt
to restore original conditions.  RECLAIMATION: The process of reconverting
land to other  forms of productive uses.  REVEGETATION: Reestablishment
of vegetation which may take  place naturally or be induced by humans
through seeding or transplanting.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
