<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1bf8f27a-d6ff-4cb6-acb7-7e5cce11e029">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/14802b53-b702-438f-8c8a-f51506807ce6"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Birds, of the class Aves, are warm-blooded craniates with a body covering
of feathers; typically with forelimbs modified as wings for active flight.
They are free living (most can fly) in all terrestrial and surface water
habitats; some are capable of swimming underwater.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
