add broader relation (MENTAL HEALTH IMPACTS [3ad043a9-2ec8-401d-a727-5589a303ea4a,368955] - PUBLIC HEALTH [da2c70fd-d92b-45be-b159-b2c10cb387c6,83869]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Mental health refers to the emotional, psychological, and social
well-being of one or more people. 1 Mental health can be be impacted
by exposure to climate related or weather-related disasters. 2 Specific
groups of people are at higher risk for distress and other adverse
mental health consequences including but not limited to children, the
elderly, and people with preexisting mental illness. 3</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">MENTAL HEALTH IMPACTS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx124"/>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PSYCHOLOGICAL HEALTH IMPACTS</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx124">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<text xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" xml:lang="en">Adapted from (1) the CDC (https://www.cdc.gov/mentalhealth/learn/index.htm), (2) Finding 8.1 (https://health2016.globalchange.gov/mental-health-and-well-being#finding-59), and (3) and Finding 8.2 (https://health2016.globalchange.gov/mental-health-and-well-being#finding-60) of The Impacts of Climate Change on Human Health in the United States: A Scientific Assessment</text>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/e5b724af-b661-406a-ae1f-7cd2730c0576">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/b41894fa-2e3e-475b-b8f0-b6ffdd2d6e9c"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Any measurement related to the science and art of the organization
and operation of animal/livestock/poultry systems so as to obtain a
predetermined set of goals (e.g. profit maximization, sustainability,
conservation of biodiversity, etc...). Includes, but not limited to,
grazing systems, pasture systems, feedlot management, roost management,
shepherding, etc...</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ANIMAL MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx125"/>
</rdf:Description>

