<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1e7daefd-fa73-4561-90cc-478ca37bcb9a">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/0cff6e4b-e42a-4565-89ff-350adf41ed69"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-08-20 09:02:04.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A landform, often referred to as a drowned river valley. Rias are almost always estuaries. Rias form where sea levels rise relative to the land either as a result of eustatic sea level change (where the global sea levels rise), or isostatic sea level change (where the local land sinks).
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-08-06 08:16:41.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
