	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-08-16 10:21:19.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Broad, low-relief volcanic crater that is caused by a phreatomagmatic eruption, an explosion  caused by groundwater coming into contact with hot lava or magma. A maar characteristically fills with water to form a relatively shallow crater lake.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Broad, low-relief volcanic crater that is caused by a phreatomagmatic eruption, an explosion  caused by groundwater coming into contact with hot lava or magma. A maar characteristically fills with water to form a relatively shallow crater lake.</definition>
