add broader relation (HYDROGEN PEROXIDE [75662ed3-35c5-41ee-abba-51ce435d1b31,836052] - OXYGEN COMPOUNDS [4cc9b4fa-5097-447f-914c-eb90820938c6,832532]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Hydrogen peroxide is a chemical compound with the formula H2O 2. In its pure form, it is a very pale blue[5] liquid, slightly more viscous than water.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
