	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The science that treats the general configuration of the Earth's surface, specifically the study of the classification, description, nature, origin, and development of present landforms and their relationships to underlying structures, and of the history of geologic changes as recorded by these surface features.</definition>
