	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-03-15 08:44:21.0 [mgenazzi] Definition added 
insert Definition (id: null
text: Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Chiroptera. Bats forelimbs form wedded wings with long spread-out digits covered by a thin membrane flapped in flying making them the only mammals capable of sustained flight. Bats have a highly adapted lung system, use echolocation as they have poorly developed eyes and most are nocturnal
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Chiroptera. Bats forelimbs form wedded wings with long spread-out digits covered by a thin membrane flapped in flying making them the only mammals capable of sustained flight. Bats have a highly adapted lung system, use echolocation as they have poorly developed eyes and most are nocturnal</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">BATS</prefLabel>
