	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-09-05 09:44:50.0 [epneff]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: In thermodynamics, the conversion of kinetic energy into heat by work
done&amp;nbsp;against the viscous stresses in the boundary layer.&amp;nbsp;
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-10-16 19:02:27.0 [saritz] updated definition 
update Definition (Derived from Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2013); 
update Definition (Air temperature measured within the the bottom layer (atmospheric boundary layer) of the troposphere that is in contact with the surface of the earth.); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-09-04 14:41:56.0 [epneff] Insert Concept 
