	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The degree to which an electrical current can pass through water due to
ions dissolved in the water. Salinity is often calculated from
conductivity and temperature.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
