<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a9b89557-c09f-4a4a-a1eb-47c632f8eb59">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/7b98fcc5-4465-45c8-a647-557432276844"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-03-06 15:25:53.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (CARBON DIOXIDE [a9b89557-c09f-4a4a-a1eb-47c632f8eb59,83563] - GASES [7b98fcc5-4465-45c8-a647-557432276844,310625]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-03-06 15:26:52.0 [tstevens]  
update PrefLabel (DISSOLVED CARBON DIOXIDE); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-03-06 15:29:26.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Naturally present as a result of animal respiration, the decay of organic matter, and the decomposition of certain minerals. It is the major source of acidity in unpolluted water samples. Surface waters typically contain less than 10 ppm (mg/L) dissolved CO2, while ground waters, particularly if deep, may contain several hundred ppm (mg/L).); 
update Definition (Houghton, J. 1997. Global Warming: The Complete Briefing, 2nd. ed. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK. Maunder, W.J. 1994. Dictionary of Global Climate Change, 2nd ed. Chapman and Hall, NY. ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Naturally present as a result of animal respiration, the decay of organic matter, and the decomposition of certain minerals. It is the major source of acidity in unpolluted water samples. Surface waters typically contain less than 10 ppm (mg/L) dissolved CO2, while ground waters, particularly if deep, may contain several hundred ppm (mg/L).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">DISSOLVED CARBON DIOXIDE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1072"/>
</rdf:Description>

