</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-12 11:45:21.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (CIRRUS/SYSTEMS [8ce319a5-9b49-49e3-8981-3ce512c7efb0,82147] - CIRRUS KELVIN-HELMHOLTZ COLOMBIAH [d6ba91a1-a5f4-47e3-9485-89348235acb9,82149]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-20 15:53:10.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A principal cloud type, forming in the high levels of the troposphere, composed of ice crystals which appear from the ground as white tufts or filaments. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as CI.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-12 11:35:03.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (CIRRUS/SYSTEMS [8ce319a5-9b49-49e3-8981-3ce512c7efb0,82147] - TROPOSPHERIC/HIGH-LEVEL CLOUDS (OBSERVED/ANALYZED) [705cd3a0-ea07-40c8-bfa1-9c26f22d13ba,82123]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A principal cloud type, forming in the high levels of the troposphere, composed of ice crystals which appear from the ground as white tufts or filaments. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as CI.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">CIRRUS/SYSTEMS</prefLabel>
