add broader relation (FREEZE/THAW [f7849055-fa5c-437c-a8c6-08c7db3a3b0a,82789] - GLACIAL PROCESSES [d7b62912-5970-46b1-be45-6a603c9a6979,82723]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-05 08:54:31.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (FREEZE/THAW [f7849055-fa5c-437c-a8c6-08c7db3a3b0a,82789] - BASAL ICE FREEZING [a72c8430-0b33-4167-b189-1309cc2048c5,82791]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-04-01 10:58:35.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The process where water seeps into a crack in a rock, as the temperature drops below freezing, the water freezes and expands causing the crack to enlarge. The ice then melts into water again as the temperature rises above freezing. This action is repeated until the rock breaks.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The process where water seeps into a crack in a rock, as the temperature drops below freezing, the water freezes and expands causing the crack to enlarge. The ice then melts into water again as the temperature rises above freezing. This action is repeated until the rock breaks.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">FREEZE/THAW</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2755"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a72c8430-0b33-4167-b189-1309cc2048c5"/>
</rdf:Description>

