	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2019-03-12 10:30:51.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (Urban Heat Island [5ce8b673-cdb9-4000-ad00-774d1c67c1b1,368539] - ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH FACTORS [5a47842e-785d-4cc4-b1c1-2147a9252c19,84159]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The tendency for higher air temperatures to persist in urban areas as aresult of heat absorbed and emitted by buildings and asphalt, tending to make cities warmer than the surrounding countryside.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Urban Heat Island</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2673"/>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">UHI</altLabel>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Urban Heat Island Effect</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

