<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1488b98d-6497-48b9-88db-6ee82a2e3ed3"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:18:10.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - ANABATIC WINDS [5f55961d-45b8-4330-8eee-0b9a9eb4f309,278919]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-21 12:56:19.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Orographic effects include both dynamic, in which mountains disturb or distort an existing approach flow, and thermodynamic, in which heating or cooling of mountain-slope surfaces generates flow. Dynamic effects include aerodynamic obstacle effects, mountain waves, channeling, orographic blocking, and processes leading to foehn, bora, and gap winds. Thermodynamic effects include anabatic winds, katabatic winds, valley breezes, and mountain breezes.); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:11:56.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - LOCAL WINDS [1488b98d-6497-48b9-88db-6ee82a2e3ed3,278859]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-21 11:45:06.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Orographic effects include both dynamic, in which mountains disturb or distort an existing approach flow, and thermodynamic, in which heating or cooling of mountain-slope surfaces generates flow. Dynamic effects include aerodynamic obstacle effects, mountain waves, channeling, orographic blocking, and processes leading to foehn, bora, and gap winds. Thermodynamic effects include anabatic winds, katabatic winds, valley breezes, and mountain breezes.  [Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society]
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:17:11.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - FOEHN WINDS [c19501d9-bd86-4611-bd30-6a34dc763a35,278911]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:17:21.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - BORA WINDS [2cf573dd-0ed7-4455-a233-5987b5a8b52a,278913]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:17:38.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - MOUNTAIN BREEZES [6520897f-c6b6-432e-b7d5-e99b33e6932e,278915]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:17:54.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - VALLEY BREEZES [4d005bfc-597b-4a99-971f-21d3d44b7b91,278917]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 15:16:55.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (OROGRAPHIC WINDS [a1df1d50-dd2b-4944-bda5-0cf1127e2f49,278903] - KATABATIC WINDS [d7d48399-62ac-4eca-9c09-14b9094a9444,278909]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Orographic effects include both dynamic, in which mountains disturb or distort an existing approach flow, and thermodynamic, in which heating or cooling of mountain-slope surfaces generates flow. Dynamic effects include aerodynamic obstacle effects, mountain waves, channeling, orographic blocking, and processes leading to foehn, bora, and gap winds. Thermodynamic effects include anabatic winds, katabatic winds, valley breezes, and mountain breezes.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">OROGRAPHIC WINDS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx306"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5f55961d-45b8-4330-8eee-0b9a9eb4f309"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/6520897f-c6b6-432e-b7d5-e99b33e6932e"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/4d005bfc-597b-4a99-971f-21d3d44b7b91"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/c19501d9-bd86-4611-bd30-6a34dc763a35"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/2cf573dd-0ed7-4455-a233-5987b5a8b52a"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d7d48399-62ac-4eca-9c09-14b9094a9444"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1488b98d-6497-48b9-88db-6ee82a2e3ed3">
