	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Peroxyacetyl nitrate is an unstable, highly oxygenated compound that exists only in the atmosphere. It is a key intermediate in the formation of the air pollutant ozone.</definition>
