</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">is the percentage of each pixel in satellite imagery or each gridbox in a weather or climate model that is covered with clouds. A cloud fraction of one means the pixel is completely covered with clouds, while a cloud fraction of zero represents a totally cloud free pixel.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
