	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Heat flux is the amount of heat that is transferred across a surface of&#xD;
unit area in a unit of time. Also refers to latent and sensible heat&#xD;
fluxes in the atmosphere and between the Earth's surface and&#xD;
atmosphere.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
