update Definition (Soil formed in either mineral or organic materials having permafrost either within 1 m below the surface or, if the soil is strongly cryoturbated, with 2 m below the surface, and having a mean annual ground temperature below 0 deg C.); 
update Definition (National Snow and Ice Data Center (NSIDC). "http://nsidc.org" ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Soil formed in either mineral or organic materials having permafrost either within 1 m below the surface or, if the soil is strongly cryoturbated, with 2 m below the surface, and having a mean annual ground temperature below 0 deg C.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
