	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Flowering Plants are all included within the class Angiospermae.
Today angiosperms are the dominant plant life, their survival helped by
the angiosperms' flowers (through pollination), fruit (by being carried to
new places), and seeds (which contain food to nourish the young plant).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
