	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Heat transferred from the earth's molten core to under-ground deposits of dry steam (steam with no water droplets), wet steam (a mixture of steam and water droplets), hot water, or rocks lying fairly close to the earth's surface.</definition>
