<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/dc02e5fb-9ff3-483d-8c33-18db25a07eea">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5237fae3-c98e-4d4a-9013-d7c824b3862b"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-26 15:09:10.0 [gee-cee] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ISOTOPES [dc02e5fb-9ff3-483d-8c33-18db25a07eea,40043] - OCEAN/LAKE RECORDS [5237fae3-c98e-4d4a-9013-d7c824b3862b,40027]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-07-24 15:51:42.0 [mpmorahan]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signatures in ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and apply those findings to the Earth's climate at the time period in question. Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimatic signatures from corals and from benthic forams.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
