update Definition ("Phytoplankton is the plant portion of the plankton, the plant community
in marine and freshwater situations, that floats free in the water and
contains many species of algae and diatoms.); 
update Definition (Krebs, Charles K. Ecology - 4th ed. 1994.  HarperCollins College Publishers, New York, New York. ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">"Phytoplankton is the plant portion of the plankton, the plant community
in marine and freshwater situations, that floats free in the water and
contains many species of algae and diatoms.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
