</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-07-02 08:51:29.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: An atmospheric cyclonic circulation, a closed circulation.  A cyclone's direction of rotation (counterclockwise in the Northern Hemisphere) is opposite to that of an anticyclone.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">An atmospheric cyclonic circulation, a closed circulation.  A cyclone's direction of rotation (counterclockwise in the Northern Hemisphere) is opposite to that of an anticyclone.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">CYCLONES</prefLabel>
