	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The acoustic energy above which a single desired signal is heard. In
the oceans, ambient noise can be produced physically (e.g. wind, rain,
bubbles) or biologically (e.g. whales, dolphins).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
