<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/4809f1e1-1b36-46a7-a7ae-ce55523424e6">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/cda9b483-8711-42b8-82f9-e7d22ce9c62c"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Those properties which describe a satellite in its  periodic revolution.
These consist of the satellite's altitude, orbital  inclination (angle
with respect to the equator, thus a polar orbit is  near 90 degrees, while
an equatorial orbit is near 0 degrees), orbital period, etc.</definition>
