</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-02-26 08:59:06.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (ATMOSPHERIC CARBON MONOXIDE [88a1b416-1589-45a4-9923-452975ec35c7,83949] - CARBON MONOXIDE SURFACE [3965bb3f-fa0e-475e-a48c-5703c9ab9fe5,560868]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Atmospheric Carbon Monoxide (CO) is a toxic, odorless, colorless gas produced during fossil fuel or biomass burning. It is one of the longest-lived,naturally occurring atmospheric carbon compounds. The recent change in tropospheric CO content may portend a change in the balance between oxidants and reductants in the atmosphere.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ATMOSPHERIC CARBON MONOXIDE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2310"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ab3e5ad3-d2c0-4c63-b321-345307bda59d"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3965bb3f-fa0e-475e-a48c-5703c9ab9fe5"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/eb1bfadc-8aa6-477b-af6a-6c320aa21351">
