update Definition (Landforms created by the processes of wind erosion or deposition of wind
weathered surface materials. These include landforms with some of the following
geomorphic features: sand dunes, deflation hollows, and desert pavement.
Alternative spelling "aeolian landforms."); 
update Definition (Adapted from Geomorphology from Space, Chapter 8 EOLIAN LANDFORMS by Alta S.
Walker 
