	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Landforms created by the processes of wind erosion or deposition of wind
weathered surface materials. These include landforms with some of the following
geomorphic features: sand dunes, deflation hollows, and desert pavement.
Alternative spelling "aeolian landforms."</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">AEOLIAN LANDFORMS</prefLabel>
