	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-05 09:42:31.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (POROSITY [07f6c977-077b-47f2-962c-00dadcd9f555,82889] - KARST PROCESSES [63846997-4a3f-41e1-9241-6d5053360d7a,82869]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-04-01 14:07:25.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A measure of a rock's ability to hold a fluid. Mathematically, porosity is the open space in a rock divided by the total rock volume (solid +  space or holes). Porosity is normally expressed as a percentage of the total rock which is taken up by pore space.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A measure of a rock's ability to hold a fluid. Mathematically, porosity is the open space in a rock divided by the total rock volume (solid +  space or holes). Porosity is normally expressed as a percentage of the total rock which is taken up by pore space.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">POROSITY</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx493"/>
