</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Changes in crystal-orientation fabric, changes in conductivity or changes in the amount of bubbles (respectively density) are considered to cause internal reflections in glaciers and ice sheets</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
