	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Carbon dioxide capture and storage (CCS) is a process consisting of the separation of carbon dioxide from industrial and energy-related sources, transport to a storage location, and long-term isolation from the atmosphere.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
