	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-29 13:34:14.0 [tbs1979]  
update Definition (Any measurement or statistic of, related, or based on the production, distribution, and consumption of goods and services related to agriculture, food, the environment, and rural development.); 
update Definition (Adapted from: Websters Ninth New Collegiate Dictionary, 1989, Merriam-Webster, Springfield, Massachusetts, USA. ); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Any measurement or statistic of, related, or based on the production, distribution, and consumption of goods and services related to agriculture, food, the environment, and rural development.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">AGRICULTURE PRODUCTION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx514"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/941c691a-3bff-4c58-854a-16c5529524e9"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/941c691a-3bff-4c58-854a-16c5529524e9">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/83741fb9-6f86-4670-abbb-c1f3b14a939d"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-29 13:36:28.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The agricultural practice of producing or growing one single crop over a wide area. It is widely used in modern industrial agriculture  and its implementation has allowed for large harvests from minimal labor. However, monocultures can lead to the quicker spread of diseases, where a uniform crop is susceptible to a pathogen.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-26 15:34:00.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (MONOCULTURE [941c691a-3bff-4c58-854a-16c5529524e9,40097] - AGRICULTURE PRODUCTION [83741fb9-6f86-4670-abbb-c1f3b14a939d,22393]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The agricultural practice of producing or growing one single crop over a wide area. It is widely used in modern industrial agriculture  and its implementation has allowed for large harvests from minimal labor. However, monocultures can lead to the quicker spread of diseases, where a uniform crop is susceptible to a pathogen.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">MONOCULTURE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2437"/>
</rdf:Description>

