</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-21 09:26:50.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (SEA SURFACE TOPOGRAPHY [68f93a0c-1525-4f5a-9545-5d94191a3dbf,775007] - MEAN SEA SURFACE [70082342-c777-49e9-88e5-a4a77728d3cc,778239]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-22 12:44:26.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (To measure sea surface height, or surface topography, scientists need
to obtain the precise distance between the satellite and the center of
the Earth and the precise distance between the satellite and the sea
surface. Sea surface height is then calculated by subtracting the
distance between the sea surface and the satellite from the distance
between the center of the Earth and the satellite. The distance between
the satellite and the center of the Earth is obtained by carefully
monitoring the satellite position at all times.); 
update Definition (https://www.noaa.gov/); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-11-02 09:41:25.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (SEA SURFACE TOPOGRAPHY [68f93a0c-1525-4f5a-9545-5d94191a3dbf,789416] - OCEANS [91697b7d-8f2b-4954-850e-61d5f61c867d,789226]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-21 09:24:09.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (SEA SURFACE TOPOGRAPHY [68f93a0c-1525-4f5a-9545-5d94191a3dbf,775007] - SEA ICE [d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3,774840]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-21 09:22:43.0 [tstevens] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (SEA SURFACE TOPOGRAPHY [68f93a0c-1525-4f5a-9545-5d94191a3dbf,775007] - DYNAMIC TOPOGRAPHY [940550d2-1d9f-4c28-b9ba-857c2dc8ef95,778236]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">To measure sea surface height, or surface topography, scientists need
to obtain the precise distance between the satellite and the center of
the Earth and the precise distance between the satellite and the sea
surface. Sea surface height is then calculated by subtracting the
distance between the sea surface and the satellite from the distance
between the center of the Earth and the satellite. The distance between
the satellite and the center of the Earth is obtained by carefully
monitoring the satellite position at all times.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">SEA SURFACE TOPOGRAPHY</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2320"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/9ac7a1c5-4179-47bc-8589-ebaa90d6cbd1"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5c0b448c-7eb4-4e8c-8403-260cbb6114bb"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/940550d2-1d9f-4c28-b9ba-857c2dc8ef95"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/70082342-c777-49e9-88e5-a4a77728d3cc"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/52a32bd3-d701-49e1-a827-67b3d96d8e56"/>
</rdf:Description>

