	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Molecules that form the basis of gene expression. The flow of information from DNA to RNA to proteins is one of the fundamental principles of molecular biology. It is so important that it is sometimes called the “central dogma.”</definition>
