	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-05 10:14:24.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (HYDROGEN GAS [96bbae63-81c1-43b4-90f0-52731e2b52ca,82907] - HYDROGEN GAS VERTICAL/GEOGRAPHIC DISTRIBUTION [833b6958-fc93-473c-aadb-bb65da7578e5,82911]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-05 10:12:33.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (HYDROGEN GAS [96bbae63-81c1-43b4-90f0-52731e2b52ca,82907] - EARTH GASES/LIQUIDS [e3fa1998-b003-4d55-a92e-16b42ac0fc17,61689]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-11 12:34:20.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Hydrogen gas is colorless, odorless, tasteless, flammable, and nontoxic. Hydrogen gas exists as a gas at ambient temperatures and atmospheric pressures. Hydrogen gas is the lightest gas known with a density approximately 0.07 that of air. The concentration of hydrogen gas in the atmosphere volume is 5.0 x 10-5%. Hydrogen is principally shipped and used in gaseous form for refineries, petrochemical companies for hydrotreating, catalytic reforming and hydrocracking. Hydrogen is also used in heat treating, metal production, welding, lasers, plastics, food production, and semiconductors.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Hydrogen gas is colorless, odorless, tasteless, flammable, and nontoxic. Hydrogen gas exists as a gas at ambient temperatures and atmospheric pressures. Hydrogen gas is the lightest gas known with a density approximately 0.07 that of air. The concentration of hydrogen gas in the atmosphere volume is 5.0 x 10-5%. Hydrogen is principally shipped and used in gaseous form for refineries, petrochemical companies for hydrotreating, catalytic reforming and hydrocracking. Hydrogen is also used in heat treating, metal production, welding, lasers, plastics, food production, and semiconductors.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">HYDROGEN GAS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2323"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/833b6958-fc93-473c-aadb-bb65da7578e5"/>
</rdf:Description>

