	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The height ascribed to the lowest layer of clouds or obscurring phenomena
when it is reported as broken (5/8 to 7/8 coverage), overcast, or obscuration
and not classified "thin" or "partial".  Expressed in above ground level (AGL)
heights. See also the definitions for cloud height and cloud base.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
