add broader relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - TROPICAL CYCLONES [06180441-d4bb-4fed-b36a-9b3cb2cac0fe,217775]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2016-07-31 20:05:40.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - SEVERE TROPICAL CYCLONES (SW PACIFIC/SE INDIAN) [5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1,247565]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2016-06-28 15:12:42.0 [saritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2016-07-31 20:05:21.0 [saritz] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE [38cefcb2-f5d6-4917-a87b-7cfba482e30d,217795] - TYPHOONS (WESTERN N. PACIFIC) [cfb85bf2-9920-4e3f-bce3-3d8f68ab1436,247563]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The atmospheric pressure at the center of a high or low.  It is the highest pressure in a high and the lowest pressure in a low, referring to the sea level pressure of the system.   In a hurricane, a lower central pressure create a stronger gradient from outside to inside the system.  The stronger this pressure gradient is, the greater the maximum wind speeds around the eye wall.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">MINIMUM CENTRAL PRESSURE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1217"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5b70e02b-0ed2-42a0-9fe9-7a552d6819d1"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ef467c3c-0aed-4aa8-bfa5-67721e83e557"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/cfb85bf2-9920-4e3f-bce3-3d8f68ab1436"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/50abff20-11a8-4aea-8425-c9a05b1d8d09"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3b1544bc-1711-4553-a643-5d8fba38a1f1"/>
</rdf:Description>

