insert Definition (id: null
text: Deoxyribonucleic acid (abbreviated DNA) is the double-stranded molecule that carries genetic information for the development and functioning of an organism. Whole extracted DNA from an organism or environment often referred to as gDNA (genomic).
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Deoxyribonucleic acid (abbreviated DNA) is the double-stranded molecule that carries genetic information for the development and functioning of an organism. Whole extracted DNA from an organism or environment often referred to as gDNA (genomic).</definition>
