	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Surface relief of the land. Topography usually is measured in meters above sea&#xD;
level. The topography can be very different from one location to another.&#xD;
Topography can be flat, or mountainous, or hilly.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">GLACIER TOPOGRAPHY/ICE SHEET TOPOGRAPHY</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1000"/>
</rdf:Description>

