	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A continuous sheet of land ice that covers a very large area and moves outward&#xD;
in many directions. &#xD;
This type of ice mass is so thick as to mask the land surface contours, in&#xD;
contrast to the smaller and thinner highland ice. The continental glacier of&#xD;
Greenland is sometimes called the Inland Ice. This term is often used to&#xD;
describe the great ice masses that characterized the ice ages.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ICE SHEETS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1033"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/94402f47-38ea-4798-98da-ea17599e092f"/>
