</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Earth Radiation Budget is the balance between incoming energy from the sun and the outgoing longwave (thermal) and reflected shortwave energy from the Earth.

[Source: Department of Marine and Coastal Sciences, Rutgers University, https://marine.rutgers.edu/cool/education/class/yuri/erb.html]</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">EARTH RADIATION BUDGET</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx721"/>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">EARTH ENERGY BUDGET</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

