	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-11 13:34:25.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The measure of Isotopes, atoms that contain different # of proton /neutrons. The number of protons (the atomic number) is the same for each isotope, e.g. carbon-12, carbon-13 and carbon-14 each have 6 protons, but the number of neutrons in each isotope differs.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-18 08:19:33.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (ISOTOPE MEASUREMENTS [849edfe2-9ed7-4211-8f57-9c8ccff0a4ea,82363] - GEOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES [048df94e-841d-4f4d-a5c5-6683d1d07aa6,82357]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The measure of Isotopes, atoms that contain different # of proton /neutrons. The number of protons (the atomic number) is the same for each isotope, e.g. carbon-12, carbon-13 and carbon-14 each have 6 protons, but the number of neutrons in each isotope differs.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ISOTOPE MEASUREMENTS</prefLabel>
