	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Geomagnetic indices are an indicator of geomagntic activity caused by solar&#xD;
events. Typical geomagntic indices are: a, A, Ap, Dst, K, and Kp.   The
A-index,&#xD;
for example, is a daily average composed of 3-hour data points.  Geomagnetic&#xD;
indices can be used in conjunction with solar"wind" data to predict the onset&#xD;
and intensity of geomagnetic storms.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">GEOMAGNETIC INDICES</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx734"/>
</rdf:Description>

