	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The genus amoebae includes several protozoan species.  Although, through
the microscope it appears as a shapeless mass of cytoplasm surrounded by a
thin membrane.  Amoebae perform all of life's functions.</definition>
