	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Refers to the distribution and size of the pyroclastic elements when they are erupted from a volcano. In moving pyroclastic systems, particles are sorted as a function of their sizes, densities and shapes. The analysis of the distribution of these characteristics in particle populations of pyroclastic deposits is a major tool in evaluating properties and regimes of parent transport systems.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PYROCLASTIC PARTICAL SIZE DISTRIBUTION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1620"/>
</rdf:Description>

