	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Paleovegetation refers to plant species that were living at some time in the
past. Indicators of past vegetation include pollen and plant macrofossils.
Animal fossils and sedimentary indicators can also be used to reconstruct past
vegetation.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
