insert Definition (id: null
text: The Tropospheric Water Vapor Lidar emits 355nm light using an NdYag pulsed laser.   The 355 nm Raman shifted backscatter light from nitrogen and water vapor are measured and used to calculate a vertically resolved profile of Water Vapor Mixing ratios.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Tropospheric Water Vapor Lidar emits 355nm light using an NdYag pulsed laser.   The 355 nm Raman shifted backscatter light from nitrogen and water vapor are measured and used to calculate a vertically resolved profile of Water Vapor Mixing ratios.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">WATER VAPOR MIXING RATIO PROFILES</prefLabel>
