add broader relation (OXYGEN ISOTOPES [a1362cee-634d-40f4-b47f-901b328895c3,106771] - ISOTOPES [a0358b3e-0926-4b17-8b32-c1b15a73cba5,87287]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Naturally occurring oxygen is composed of threestable isotopes, 16O, 17O, and 18O, with 16O being the most abundant (99.762% natural abundance)</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
