	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The process by which a solid or liquid forms a solution in a solvent. In solids this can be explained as the breakdown of the crystal lattice into individual ions, atoms or molecules and their transport into the solvent.</definition>
