add broader relation (CALIBRATION [ecf29317-bd5e-447b-b911-f8bfb153c83b,309609] - CALIBRATION/VALIDATION [4f938731-d686-4d89-b72b-ff60474bb1f0,86319]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Calibration is defined as Data Analysis and Visualization Service that is designed to allow a user of the service to properly adjust Earth science data to achieve optimal accuracy and/or precision. EXAMPLE: An algorithm to correct for the decaying orbit of a satellite (calibration).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
