	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">An ecosystem within a landscape defined as Karst topography characterized by&#xD;
caves, sinkholes, disappraring streams and underground drainage. Karst forms&#xD;
when groundwater dissolves pockets of limestone, dolomite, or gypsum in rock.</definition>
