	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A type of frozen precipitation composed of white or translucent ice
crystals, chiefly in complex branch hexagonal form and often agglomerated
into snow-flakes, especially at temperatures warmer than -5 C (23
F).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
