	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The soil profile is the vertical section of the soil, from the surface
through all its horizons, where a horizon is a layer of soil,
approximately parallel to the soil surface, differing in properties and
characteristics from adjacent layers below and above it.</definition>
