	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The physical process by which a liquid is transformed to the gaseous
state. Evaporation also implies a loss of heat from the ocean surface and
is an important term in determining the heat budget of the ocean.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
