	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/da2c70fd-d92b-45be-b159-b2c10cb387c6"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2019-04-03 12:18:29.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (WATER TREATMENT DISRUPTION [91df78a1-2e38-41d5-b88e-e235450c89fc,368615] - PUBLIC HEALTH [da2c70fd-d92b-45be-b159-b2c10cb387c6,83869]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Disruption to the normal treatment of drinking water, wastewater, or stormwater that can reduce drinking water availability and potentially increase human exposure to waterborne chemicals, pathogens, and toxins. Water treatment disruption can be a result of aging infrastructure and/or extreme weather.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">WATER TREATMENT DISRUPTION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1788"/>
</rdf:Description>

