	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-10-03 09:07:47.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Any non-linear shaped opening enclosed by ice. May contain brash ice and/or
be covered with new ice, nilas or young ice; sub-mariners refer to these
as skylights. Polynyas are important in the study of the energy budget of
the polar ocean and local and regional climatology.); 
update Definition (Canadian Ice Service - Environment Canada
"http://www.cis.ec.gc.ca/manice/chp1_eng.htm" 
See also Hall, D.K. and J. Martinec. 1985. Remote Sensing of Ice and Snow,
Chapman and Hall. London.); 
insert WeightedRelation (id: null
related concept uuid: 70acf223-7895-4cbe-aca6-815babb2b7ed
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Any non-linear shaped opening enclosed by ice. May contain brash ice and/or
be covered with new ice, nilas or young ice; sub-mariners refer to these
as skylights. Polynyas are important in the study of the energy budget of
the polar ocean and local and regional climatology.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">POLYNYAS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2825"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ea85ea0b-1b7d-464a-9f8c-1f80383ffc51">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-10-03 09:00:04.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (Pack ice refers to high concentrations of sea ice. When concentrations are
60% or less, then the term drift ice is used.); 
insert WeightedRelation (id: null
related concept uuid: 5d7ea074-225b-4221-b122-e6a085cdce24
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Pack ice refers to high concentrations of sea ice. When concentrations are
60% or less, then the term drift ice is used.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PACK ICE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1531"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/9d99408d-0d8b-4642-a2cb-edee8319fe1d">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Isotopes are a form of an element with a certain number of neutrons, for&#xD;
example carbon exists in three isotopes: C12, C13, and C14. Some isotopes are&#xD;
naturally unstable and spontaneously decay at a fixed rate; other isotopes are&#xD;
stable.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ISOTOPES</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx3122"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/1151dc7e-7441-4a21-95b6-1d03a1053f60">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A piece of ice that has broken off from the end of a glacier that terminates in
water. Only about 10 percent of its mass is above the surface of the water.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ICEBERGS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2899"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/a47ab696-7ed9-4374-8965-c8996e61463d">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-21 09:33:39.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (SEA ICE MOTION [a47ab696-7ed9-4374-8965-c8996e61463d,774858] - SEA ICE SPEED [ad4646f8-bf09-4751-9072-e6cec59af253,778241]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-10-21 09:31:59.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (SEA ICE MOTION [a47ab696-7ed9-4374-8965-c8996e61463d,774858] - SEA ICE DIRECTION [ab411758-5abe-4a89-9319-97eba1510cda,778240]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Refers to the movement and direction of ice fields or floes. Ice&#xD;
motion processes include: diverging, compacting, and shearing.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">SEA ICE MOTION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2970"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ad4646f8-bf09-4751-9072-e6cec59af253"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ab411758-5abe-4a89-9319-97eba1510cda"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/4519a99a-ffa7-436b-888a-c742c82b9ed1">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2023-02-24 12:27:46.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (SEA ICE MASS BALANCE [4519a99a-ffa7-436b-888a-c742c82b9ed1,1232204] - SEA ICE [d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3,1228717]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-10-03 09:39:11.0 [tstevens]  
insert WeightedRelation (id: null
related concept uuid: cfc3ed52-a7e2-4ad1-8330-1f97c7cb0203
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2023-02-24 12:28:37.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The net balance between the sea ice mass gained by freezing and the loss of mass by melting that is a function of its extent and thickness, which combine to give its volume.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The net balance between the sea ice mass gained by freezing and the loss of mass by melting that is a function of its extent and thickness, which combine to give its volume.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">SEA ICE MASS BALANCE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2839"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/8ed9f39d-986e-4b36-83f9-f29f6a4df89b">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The reflectance properties of ice bodies. A smooth ice surface will act as&#xD;
a near-specular reflector. As surface roughness increases, the reflection&#xD;
becomes diffuse. It is the ratio of the intensity of reflected radiation&#xD;
to that of the incident radiation on a surface. The suffix (-ance) implies&#xD;
a property of that particular specimen surface.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">REFLECTANCE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1857"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/2a664e2d-4e50-463a-af9f-b14b86eb42a7">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73e969a-4b66-4713-8d63-fa3cbb1e25e3"/>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Measurements of the temperature of the sea ice and surrounding sea
surface temperature. These measurements are usually obtained from remote
sensing satellites.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ICE TEMPERATURE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1409"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/defd2c00-64e3-4986-9061-feade19f972f">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
