	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-10-25 10:07:30.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: Sea ice advection is the movement of sea ice and is a function of the following factors: atmosphere-ice and ice-ocean momentum stress and sea surface gradient.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Sea ice advection is the movement of sea ice and is a function of the following factors: atmosphere-ice and ice-ocean momentum stress and sea surface gradient.</definition>
