</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A glacial lake is a body of water with origins from glacier activity. They are formed when a glacier erodes the land, and then melts, filling the depression created by the glacier.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">GLACIAL LAKE EXTENT</prefLabel>
	<altLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">GLACIAL LAKES</altLabel>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/f956cc7c-da39-4eac-98ab-ba6207181b7d">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/5cef2f41-a17a-4eff-8ce4-328593e1b703"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-18 08:00:24.0 [tbs1979] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (MINERAL DISSOLUTION [f956cc7c-da39-4eac-98ab-ba6207181b7d,82343] - MARINE GEOCHEMICAL PROCESSES [1dd9be28-df7b-434f-bea1-5b171d09312b,82341]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-03-11 13:48:45.0 [tbs1979]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The separation of minerals into different components. Mineral dissolution and precipitation, especially of Fe and Mn (hydr)oxides and the carbonate mineral family, partially regulate pH and alkalinity of natural waters, affecting the fate and transport of organic and inorganic contaminants.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-18 08:02:53.0 [tbs1979] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (MINERAL DISSOLUTION [f956cc7c-da39-4eac-98ab-ba6207181b7d,82343] - MARINE GEOCHEMISTRY [5cef2f41-a17a-4eff-8ce4-328593e1b703,64123]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The separation of minerals into different components. Mineral dissolution and precipitation, especially of Fe and Mn (hydr)oxides and the carbonate mineral family, partially regulate pH and alkalinity of natural waters, affecting the fate and transport of organic and inorganic contaminants.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">MINERAL DISSOLUTION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1189"/>
</rdf:Description>

