	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Physical and laboratory models are models that represent a larger or smaller physical copy of an object or structure. Most commonly, these models are created in laboratories, but can often be located and studied in the real environment. Physical models allow visualization, from examining the model, of information about the thing the model represents.</definition>
