	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Natural nitrogen (N) consists of two stable isotopes, nitrogen-14, which makes up the vast majority of naturally occurring nitrogen, andnitrogen-15. Fourteen radioactive isotopes (radioisotopes) have also been found so far, with atomic masses ranging from 10 to 25, and one nuclear isomer, 11mN.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
