	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Green algae are distinguished by chlorophyll a and b proportions, accessory pigments beta-carotene, and xanthophylls in stacked thylakoids. Cell walls are typically cellulose and they store carbohydrates as starch</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">GREEN ALGAE</prefLabel>
</rdf:Description>

