</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-10-16 19:19:14.0 [saritz] updated definition 
update Definition (The temperature to which a given air parcel must be cooled at constant pressure and constant water vapor content in order for saturation to occur.); 
update Definition (Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2012, http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Dewpoint); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-09-05 09:46:56.0 [epneff]  
update Definition (Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996.); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The temperature to which a given air parcel must be cooled at constant pressure and constant water vapor content in order for saturation to occur.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
