<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/25d4368e-3b66-40d5-bac1-2343b127fa32">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/b887d3e5-4280-43d2-a34e-0f63ac086b6a"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-25 10:42:39.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add narrower relation (MADDEN-JULIAN OSCILLATION [25d4368e-3b66-40d5-bac1-2343b127fa32,22989] - MJO [2953da71-fe1d-4506-9bd6-445b92e2b443,39709]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2020-02-14 15:05:12.0 [tstevens] Remove Concepts 
delete narrower relation (null); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">In 1971 Roland Madden and Paul Julian stumbled upon a 40-50 day&#xD;
oscillation when analyzing zonal wind anomalies in the tropical&#xD;
Pacific. They used ten years of pressure records at Canton (at 2.8B0 S&#xD;
in the Pacific) and upper level winds at Singapore.&#xD;
The oscillation of surface and upper-level winds was remarkably clear&#xD;
in Singapore. Until the early 1980's little attention was paid to this&#xD;
oscillation, which became known as the Madden and Julian&#xD;
Oscillation(MJO), and some scientists questioned its global&#xD;
significance. Since the 1982-83 El Nino event, low-frequency&#xD;
variations in the tropics, both on intra-annual (less than a year) and&#xD;
inter-annual (more than a year) timescales, have received much more&#xD;
attention, and the number of MJO-related publications grew rapidly.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">MADDEN-JULIAN OSCILLATION</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1265"/>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1265">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<text xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" xml:lang="en">NOAA/NWS:&#xD;
"http://ww2.wrh.noaa.gov/climate_info/Madden-Julian_Oscillation.htm"&#xD;
For a full bibliography of MJO papers, see:&#xD;
"http://www.coaps.fsu.edu/lib/elninobib/Madden-Julian-Oscillation/"&gt;</text>
</rdf:Description>

