	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The ratio of the emittance of a given surface at a specified wavelength
and emitting temperature to the emittance of an ideal black body at the
same wavelength and temperature. Emissivity has a value between 0 (least)
and one (greatest).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
