<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d73be111-7aae-4a96-89c2-7b64c064893c">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/e8580cbb-701a-4ab1-a40f-5fae4ae1ea24"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-26 10:27:08.0 [gee-cee] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (TEMPERATURE CONCENTRATION INDEX (TCI) [d73be111-7aae-4a96-89c2-7b64c064893c,39803] - TEMPERATURE INDICES [e8580cbb-701a-4ab1-a40f-5fae4ae1ea24,39791]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-09-23 14:49:20.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A new index that is called as the temperature concentration index (TCI) was developed in the present study to investigate the concentration of temperature in Iran based on the two known inspiring patterns of Gibbs–Martin (Am Sociol Rev 27:667–677, 1962) and Oliver (Prof Geogr 32:300–309, 1980). The developed index was classified based on three methods, including the Oliver’ classification (1980), the coefficient of variation of temperature data, and coefficient of variation of TCI values. The results show that all the three classification methods represent almost similar classes for the TCI.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A new index that is called as the temperature concentration index (TCI) was developed in the present study to investigate the concentration of temperature in Iran based on the two known inspiring patterns of Gibbs–Martin (Am Sociol Rev 27:667–677, 1962) and Oliver (Prof Geogr 32:300–309, 1980). The developed index was classified based on three methods, including the Oliver’ classification (1980), the coefficient of variation of temperature data, and coefficient of variation of TCI values. The results show that all the three classification methods represent almost similar classes for the TCI.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">TEMPERATURE CONCENTRATION INDEX (TCI)</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1358"/>
</rdf:Description>

