	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Total electron content is the total vertically integrated number
of electrons per unit surface area on the earth. In standard metric
units this is 10E16 electrons/m^2 also known as a TEC unit or TECU.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
