	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Submarine canyon are relatively narrow, V-shaped, deep depression with steep
slopes, the bottom of which grades continuously downward across the continental
slope.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
