	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-14 10:40:00.0 [mpmorahan] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS [bec5166e-1822-40f7-8f07-4d5167d8a565,82253] - STRATOCUMULUS [3375096a-7782-42e8-97d2-0febf63893e0,82231]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-14 10:41:01.0 [mpmorahan] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS [bec5166e-1822-40f7-8f07-4d5167d8a565,82253] - STRATOCUMULUS LENTICULARIS [12adeea5-f3e7-4f72-a029-f1e52411de18,82251]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-14 10:40:34.0 [mpmorahan] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS [bec5166e-1822-40f7-8f07-4d5167d8a565,82253] - STRATOCUMULUS PERLUCIDUS [94fa2efc-0e7f-4dce-9f2a-0d6f34edcb92,82247]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-14 10:40:21.0 [mpmorahan] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS [bec5166e-1822-40f7-8f07-4d5167d8a565,82253] - STRATOCUMULUS OPACUS [53ade6b0-1b8c-4766-b9c1-4d40d1f69482,82245]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-02-14 10:40:42.0 [mpmorahan] Move Concepts 
add narrower relation (STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS [bec5166e-1822-40f7-8f07-4d5167d8a565,82253] - STRATOCUMULUS TRANSLUCIDUS [b962de0e-f115-4452-95be-7a4af6687bc3,82249]); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2024-10-09 10:38:46.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: A layer composed of large and often grey elements, arranged in a system of nearly parallel lines. A double system of undulations is sometimes visible in the form of transverse lines that cross the main system. The elements then appear to be arranged in “rank and file”. Stratocumulus undulatus occurs in the species stratiformis.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A layer composed of large and often grey elements, arranged in a system of nearly parallel lines. A double system of undulations is sometimes visible in the form of transverse lines that cross the main system. The elements then appear to be arranged in “rank and file”. Stratocumulus undulatus occurs in the species stratiformis.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">STRATOCUMULUS UNDULATAS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2282"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/12adeea5-f3e7-4f72-a029-f1e52411de18"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/94fa2efc-0e7f-4dce-9f2a-0d6f34edcb92"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/b962de0e-f115-4452-95be-7a4af6687bc3"/>
	<narrower xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/53ade6b0-1b8c-4766-b9c1-4d40d1f69482"/>
