<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/dd4de9c8-e078-43cf-a7d8-78f289c8618e">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ad557b31-fc70-4519-a8e4-3a5daf05f774"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-03-13 14:09:01.0 [mgenazzi] Definition added 
insert Definition (id: null
text: Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or 'reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it's soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or 'reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it's soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">HARD OR STONY CORALS</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2607"/>
</rdf:Description>

