	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A dissolved ion of carbonic acid, with the chemical formula CO3(-2), formed
by dissolution of carbon dioxide in water. Other forms of carbonate, such
as bicarbonate, HCO3-, are included with this variable as detailed
variables.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">CARBONATE</prefLabel>
</rdf:Description>

