<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/ff5d5c12-74d9-435d-9164-1c9d69f967d7">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/35e1f93b-99b3-4430-b477-0ecafa80d67a"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-10-11 17:09:19.0 [saritz] Updated definition. 
update Definition (Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996. ); 
update Definition (The property of the atmosphere, usually assumed in hydrostatic equilibrium
with respect to vertical displacements of air parcels.); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-10-11 17:10:52.0 [saritz] Updated definition. 
update Definition (The characteristic of a system if sufficiently small disturbances have only small effects, either decreasing in amplitude or oscillating periodically; it is asymptotically stable if the effect of small disturbances vanishes for long time periods.); 
update Definition (Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2012.); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The characteristic of a system if sufficiently small disturbances have only small effects, either decreasing in amplitude or oscillating periodically; it is asymptotically stable if the effect of small disturbances vanishes for long time periods.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">ATMOSPHERIC STABILITY</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1617"/>
</rdf:Description>

