	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">In radiometery, a measure of the intrinsic radiant intensity emitted by&#xD;
a radiator in a given direction. Radiance is measured in watts per square&#xD;
meter and steradian.   Units: W·sr^−1·m^−2</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">INFRARED RADIANCE</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2921"/>
