insert Definition (id: null
text: Phylum Phoronida. Commonly called Horeshoe worms are hermaphroditic, marine, benthic, suspension feeding vermiform animals distringuished with a looped digestive tract and the anus is located close to the mouth. Adult Phoronida live in chitinous tube attached or burrowed in a hard substrate with lophophore, ciliated feeding structure, surrounding the mouth.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Phylum Phoronida. Commonly called Horeshoe worms are hermaphroditic, marine, benthic, suspension feeding vermiform animals distringuished with a looped digestive tract and the anus is located close to the mouth. Adult Phoronida live in chitinous tube attached or burrowed in a hard substrate with lophophore, ciliated feeding structure, surrounding the mouth.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
