update Definition (The small-scale variation in the relief of the terrain surface (in this
case the surface of the ice). Remote sensing instruments, such as radar
and microwave sensors, have been able to detect the degree of roughness of
sea, lake, and river ice.); 
insert WeightedRelation (id: null
related concept uuid: a6c3e78f-f408-4b72-941a-f40e3d83dd60
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The small-scale variation in the relief of the terrain surface (in this
case the surface of the ice). Remote sensing instruments, such as radar
and microwave sensors, have been able to detect the degree of roughness of
sea, lake, and river ice.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
