</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Common Sense Climate Index (Hansen et al. 1998) is a simple&#xD;
measure of the degree (if any) to which practical climate change is&#xD;
occurring. The index is a composite of several everyday climate&#xD;
indicators. It is expected to have positive values when warming occurs&#xD;
and negative values for cooling. If the Index reaches and consistently&#xD;
maintains a value of 1 or more, the climate change should be&#xD;
noticeable to most people who have lived at that location for a few&#xD;
decades.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">COMMON SENSE CLIMATE INDEX</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2335"/>
</rdf:Description>

