	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Of, or pertaining to, the outer perimeter of a glacier, particularly to the&#xD;
fringe areas surrounding the great continental glaciers of the geologic ice&#xD;
ages.  Thus, periglacial weathering is said to have produced certain&#xD;
characteristic land forms.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">PERIGLACIAL PROCESSES</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx1922"/>
</rdf:Description>

