	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2020-09-29 13:28:38.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (COMMON MIDPOINT GATHER [d8b34f6e-0713-45ae-b0c7-23329b0b8f0b,560729] - RADAR BACKSCATTER [625da982-3648-43fc-a640-1b230509944e,86025]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A common midpoint (CMP) gather is constructed when multichannel surveys image the same subsurface target through multiple pathways, using a range of source‐receiver offsets. The CMP gather is a collection of all recorded offsets co-located about a single reflection point in the snow or firn.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">COMMON MIDPOINT GATHER</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx2169"/>
</rdf:Description>

