<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d7fbbafe-fc73-4b63-9837-3d53d2370d9d">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/3c4fe00c-6fb1-403e-a053-3a0174a6dfe6"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-21 12:56:33.0 [sritz]  
update Definition (In meteorological usage, this term is applied only to the transformation from vapor to liquid; any process in which a solid forms directly from its vapor is termed deposition, and the reverse process sublimation.); 
update Definition (Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-04-20 14:10:30.0 [sritz] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (CONDENSATION [d7fbbafe-fc73-4b63-9837-3d53d2370d9d,84643] - WATER VAPOR PROCESSES [3c4fe00c-6fb1-403e-a053-3a0174a6dfe6,278813]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">In meteorological usage, this term is applied only to the transformation from vapor to liquid; any process in which a solid forms directly from its vapor is termed deposition, and the reverse process sublimation.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">CONDENSATION</prefLabel>
