	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The process in which a wave or beam of particles is diffused or deflected&#xD;
by collisions with particles of the medium which it traverses. Along&#xD;
with absorption, scattering is a major cause of the attenuation of&#xD;
radiation by the atmosphere.</definition>
