	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2021-03-03 09:19:36.0 [tstevens]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: SF6- an inert gas categorized as hydrofluorocarbons, measured at the earth's surface. Sulfur hexafluoride absorbs thermal infrared radiation and could increase global warming as its concentration in the atmosphere increases; therefore it is a greenhouse gas.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">SF6- an inert gas categorized as hydrofluorocarbons, measured at the earth's surface. Sulfur hexafluoride absorbs thermal infrared radiation and could increase global warming as its concentration in the atmosphere increases; therefore it is a greenhouse gas.</definition>
