<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/d57dff3d-5f2f-425c-80bb-2a6fcb42d3fa">
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource"/>
	<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
	<broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/f36d71c6-f2ad-49c4-809f-09b4f0688412"/>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2013-08-15 14:15:10.0 [tbs1979]  
update Definition (Restoration: The processes by which an area is treated in  an attempt to restore original conditions.  

Reclamation: The process of reconverting land to other forms of productive uses.  

Revegetation: Reestablishment of vegetation which may take  place naturally or be induced by humans through seeding or transplanting.); 
update Definition (The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996.  &lt;BR&gt; Herren, R.V., and R.L. Donahue.  1991.  The Agricultural Dictionary, Delmar Publishers, INC. Albany, New York.  553pp. ); 
</changeNote>
	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2017-03-10 09:00:17.0 [tstevens]  
update Definition (The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996. Herren, R.V., and R.L. Donahue.  1991.  The Agricultural Dictionary, Delmar Publishers, INC. Albany, New York.  553pp.); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Restoration: The processes by which an area is treated in  an attempt to restore original conditions.  

Reclamation: The process of reconverting land to other forms of productive uses.  

Revegetation: Reestablishment of vegetation which may take  place naturally or be induced by humans through seeding or transplanting.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
