	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">For a given cloud or cloud layer, the lowest level in the atmosphere at which
the air contains a perceptible quantity of cloud particles.
See also the definitions for cloud height and cloud ceiling.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
