	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Depth at which a Secchi disk, when lowered into the water from the
surface, disappears from view due to turbidity of the water. Used as a
quick assessment of water clarity.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
