	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Shortwave radiation is radiation at wavelengths shorter than 4
microns. Sometimes called the solar radiation. Usually radiation in the
visible and near-infrared wavelengths.</definition>
