insert Definition (id: null
text: Refers to the variability of the canopy temperature, which is an integrative trait that reflects the plant water status or the resultant equilibrium between the root water uptake and shoot transpiration.
language code: en); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Refers to the variability of the canopy temperature, which is an integrative trait that reflects the plant water status or the resultant equilibrium between the root water uptake and shoot transpiration.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
