related concept uuid: 10a128a6-12d4-4bce-b25d-2ffc464182f4
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Any non-linear shaped opening enclosed by ice. May contain brash ice and/or
be covered with new ice, nilas or young ice; sub-mariners refer to these
as skylights. Polynyas are important in the study of the energy budget of
the polar ocean and local and regional climatology.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
