	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Surface Moisture Index incorporates remote measures of vegetation&#xD;
condition coupled with radiometric thermal (temperature) data to&#xD;
characterize surface moisture conditions. It is mapped using two&#xD;
primary inputs; vegetation status as depicted by Normalized Difference&#xD;
Vegetation Index (NDVI) and surface temperature.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
