	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2012-06-26 11:05:34.0 [gee-cee] Move Concepts 
delete broader relation (null); 
add broader relation (FOREST FIRE DANGER INDEX [16329a9b-72ea-4b46-b507-2ce389c63f50,22803] - LAND SURFACE/AGRICULTURE INDICATORS [112e71ec-c0a1-49a8-82d7-bcb317b45860,39835]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">A forest fire danger index (FDI) or burning index (BI) is a relative number&#xD;
related to the contribution that fire behavior makes to the amount of effort&#xD;
needed to contain a fire of a specified fuel type. The index may be calculated&#xD;
differently by different agencies around the world.</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
	<prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">FOREST FIRE DANGER INDEX</prefLabel>
	<reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5qapbx3192"/>
</rdf:Description>

