	<changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2019-03-13 07:47:15.0 [tstevens] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (SOLAR RADIATION MANAGEMENT [0f583845-c39e-471d-a590-8212a4358e1e,368567] - GEOENGINEERING [262e3568-c57b-4e28-a142-ad5e7b51dfb7,368563]); 
</changeNote>
	<definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">Solar Radiation Management (SRM) refers to the intentional modification of the Earth’s shortwave radiative budget with the aim to reduce climate change according to a given metric (e.g., surface temperature, precipitation, regional impacts, etc).</definition>
	<inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
